reports.QA_MASTER_REPORT=pre('SortTrip master QA report')+`## Assessment\n\n**NO-GO for unrestricted financial/booking launch. CONDITIONAL GO for limited read-only discovery/affiliate browsing**, with unverified fares clearly labelled and the restrictions in PRODUCTION_READINESS.md. QA execution/reporting is closed for this evidence snapshot; this does not certify every feature or resolve owner-controlled operations.\n\n`+stats+`\n## Findings and safe corrections\n\n${fixed.length} fix groups were implemented locally. No observed P0 in the bounded audit; this is not a security assurance or evidence that hidden vulnerabilities do not exist. Three production SEO/404 probes remain FAIL because local fixes have not been released. One local checkout readiness probe is BLOCKED.\n\n`+issueTable+`\n## Evidence and coverage limits\n\nSee QA_TEST_MATRIX.csv for each test ID, status, layer and evidence. See FEATURE_INVENTORY.md for all inventoried source files, endpoint families and database definitions. The source scan covers ${inventory.inventory.length} selected files; generated/vendor/env/secret/queue/git-history contents are excluded. All identified source control families are mapped; not every destructive/payment/login button was clicked. Those exclusions are explicit in the matrix, not assumed to work. Screenshots and sanitized JSON/TAP/build output are under 2026-10-23/evidence. Browser iframe pixels/inputs and full WCAG/CWV are not covered by the top-level layout metric.\n\n## Remaining work ownership\n\nOwner-operated controlled financial, multi-user database and messaging tests are in OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED.md. Engineering follow-ups are in FIX_LOG.md and domain reports. Source RLS and mock provider behavior do not prove deployed policy state, successful payment, supplier reservation, scheduler execution or notification receipt.\n`;
reports.FEATURE_INVENTORY=pre('Feature and architecture inventory')+mdTable(['Feature','Classification','Evidence / limit'],features)+`\n## Architecture and routes\n\nReact19/Vite8 TypeScript frontend; client sections Explore, Flights, Trip.com Hotels, Transport, My trips, Help and planner tabs. Public static routes /, /terms(.html), /privacy(.html), /404.html; /hotel-checkout SPA entry handled by Worker. Cloudflare Worker routes source adapters, Supabase auth/RLS/RPC/records, OpenAI planning/translation, Aviasales cached fares, Nuitée rates/content/SDK, Google Routes, Viator, Midtrans, Resend and separate Telegram support/agent services.\n\n`+mdTable(['Endpoint family','Responsibility'],[['/api/health','Configuration booleans, not downstream connectivity'],['/api/locations','Destination catalogue autocomplete'],['/api/flights','Indicative cached flight search'],['/api/itinerary and /translate','Authenticated planning and display translation'],['/api/hotels/search and /content','Production catalogue/rates/details/reviews'],['/api/hotels/checkout/*','Rooms/session/start/finalize/status/history; see source for action contracts'],['/api/routes/google','Explicit bounded authenticated computeRoutes'],['/api/activities/*','Viator search/health'],['/api/payments/*','Midtrans checkout/status/access/webhook'],['/api/support/*','Text tickets/messages/Telegram webhook/config'],['scheduled(event)','Hourly Price Watch, two-minute support outbox; live remote configuration not attested']])+`\n## Source/UI control inventory\n\nCounts are lexical tags, not distinct rendered controls or proof of clicking all controls. They locate every selected file for further reproduction. Repeated dynamic cards, destructive controls, owner account settings, external transactions and credential forms require the separate boundaries in the matrix.\n\n`+mdTable(['File','Lines','Interactive tags','Literal API paths'],inventory.inventory.map(x=>[x.file,x.lines,x.interactiveTags,x.apiPaths.join(', ')]))+`\n## Environment names\n\nNames only, no environment values/files read: ${inventory.environmentVariableNames.join(', ')}. Configuration/account ownership is not inferred from variable names.\n\n## Database source inventory\n\nSQL files: schema.sql; payments.sql; ai-access.sql; ai-quota-v2.sql; ai-pass-account-scope.sql; trip-pass-10.sql; trip-pass-price-30000.sql; price-watch.sql; price-watch-itinerary.sql; google-routes-budget.sql; support-chat.sql; liteapi-checkout.sql. Tables/policies/grants/RPC source index: evidence/sql-policy-index.txt. Historical files are not a safe automatic migration order.\n`;
reports.API_AUDIT=pre('API and configuration audit')+mdTable(['ID','Layer','Status','HTTP','Meaning'],[...http,...live].map(x=>[x.id,x.id.startsWith('PROD')?'production':x.id.startsWith('LOCAL')?'local':'supplier read-only',x.status,x.httpStatus,x.interpretation||x.summary?.errorKey||'Expected response/status only']))+`\n## Request and configuration boundaries\n\nInvalid/origin/unauthenticated rejection probes did not create transactions. Nonces, tokens, session identifiers and secret values were not recorded. Real searches were bounded, not bulk load. Local Viator reports sandbox and returns no products; production catalogue200 returns one product. Local Nuitée rates/content production200 but checkout503; public production checkout history401 demonstrates readiness/auth gate only. /api/health configured=true is not a real provider test. Live pricing remains date/supplier-specific. See the matrix for exact scope; provider error/retry/auth/cost controls have synthetic contracts.\n`;
reports.NUITEE_AUDIT=pre('Nuitée hotel audit')+`## Verified now\n\nFresh bounded local production search for Yogyakarta,30Jan–1Feb2027,one adult,one room,IDR100000–400000/room/night:187hotels checked,178matched before budget,47returned,partial=false,capped=true. Omah Atik totalIDR294130.31 (~147065.155/night),Cempaka308357.45 (~154178.725/night),Bring In House336273.09 (~168136.545/night). These are supplier quotes, not held stock, guaranteed lowest prices or reservations.\n\nOmah Atik content200:24photos,2room types,36facilities,10reviews. Content units/availability depend on supplier; absence is not fabricated. Cancellation RFN/NRFN, taxes, currency, total-stay vs nightly/room, occupancy and public/member price validation covered by contracts. Browser native form ID/EN passed seven widths; inverted budget rejected, clearing resets it. No hotel was saved or booked during QA.\n\n## Checkout and commercial limits\n\nNuitée API + Payment SDK is the active itinerary path. Historical owner evidence establishes form rendering from Indonesia, not a completed production reservation. Local checkout history503 reflects local readiness/configuration; production unauthenticated401 only verifies a protected enabled route. Do not reactivate approval flags, rotate keys or require White-label repair. Owner-published default5%margin is inherited; no extra frontend markup added. Actual settlement/payout unverified. LAS-3185 card liability remains a commercial question, separate from the retired White-label.\n\n## Cost controls\n\nSource endpoint allowlist blocks Places and price-index paid paths; bounded catalogue/rates sampling with at most two discovery-rate calls plus a metadata fallback, capped results; content fetch on demand; backend rate limits/validation/timeouts and adapter fixture coverage. Normal core/content pricing is described in provider documentation, but account add-ons, fair-use/look-to-book and financial terms were not independently attested. Do not promise all requests universally free. Pricing documentation reviewed earlier in this audit: https://docs.liteapi.travel/reference/api-pricing-usage-costs (Price Index examples conflict across docs; blocked here).\n\n## Remaining\n\nE2E-NUITEE-FINANCIAL requires owner-operated controlled authorization/3DS,Book,status recovery,cancel/refund and settlement. White-label branding/domain/403 are OUT OF SCOPE by latest owner direction, not failed active-path tests. Source sampling does not prove all budget hotel inventory in every city or Vietnam. Prior same-day Hanoi production quote exists in project memory; this evidence file newly repeats Yogyakarta only.\n`;
reports.FLIGHT_AUDIT=pre('Flight audit')+`## Executed\n\nFive real adapter route probes:CGK–KUL return200/0offers,CGK–SIN one-way200/2(lowest808361IDR),CGK–BKK return200/2(lowest4710978),CGK–NRT return200/0,SUB–SIN return200/0. Dates/windows are in scripts/qa-live-providers.mjs. Source: Aviasales Data API cached indicative fares, one adult. Empty cache is not sold-out availability.\n\nActual browser search exercised one-way selection,Singapore destination autocomplete, country/city/date/drilldown, flight details and duration sorting; affiliate URL inspected without purchasing. API tests cover flexible/exact dates, region/default/domestic/worldwide, invalid routes, deduplication and provider failures. Contract links preserve route/date and supported one-adult parameters. Other passenger costs are estimates unless provider says otherwise.\n\n## Corrections and limitations\n\nEnglish singular city/stops/traveller/category/CTA corrected. Default Indonesia/SEA and optional worldwide remain available. Origin autocomplete is NOT_IMPLEMENTED: current origin is fixedCGK/SUB/DPS. Final live fare/baggage/seat inventory, all filter permutations and external airline checkout are NOT_TESTED; no group fare or bookable-price guarantee. Representative routes returning no cached fares remain valid empty-result connection tests.\n`;
reports.TRANSPORT_AUDIT=pre('Transport and activities audit')+`## 12Go\n\nOfficial isolated iframe rendered origin,destination,date and Find Tickets, affiliate id in widget/fallback link. Top-level seven-width layouts passed. No native bus/train/ferry inventory API implemented: links/widget hand off search/booking. Affiliate contracts validate origin/destination/date/passenger contexts and HTTPS host safeguards. No actual seat/date fare, external checkout or commission conversion verified. Provider form remains English in Indonesian shell, an explicit vendor-language exception.\n\n## Google Routes and OSM\n\nFresh signed-in local WALK Travelodge Kuala Lumpur City Centre→KLCC Park returned44minutes/3.0km with English navigation, fare unavailable correctly distinguished from free, four personal checks remaining. One bounded request; AIquota stayed10. Modes/transit/drive/error handling tested by contracts; current liveTRANSIT/DRIVE not repeated. App caps default1000/day,9000/month and5/account/day with atomicDB counter before upstream. Other billing-project use and Google Console quotas are owner checks; no unconditional no-charge assurance.\n\nLeaflet/OSM rendered markers/stop-order lines and zoom controls. Stop-order lines are not road navigation; attribution kept. Missing-coordinate message and map-reload fallback visible. Google content stays separately attributed/temporary; no mixing Google polylines into OSM source.\n\n## Viator / Klook\n\nActual production catalogue search200/one product startingIDR832702.89; existing Genting activity retains affiliate link and from-price disclaimer. Local Viator remains sandbox/empty; configuration drift recorded. Contract tests cover source/link/price/saved-selection invalidation. Exact dated option availability and attribution settlement NOT_TESTED. Klook legacy source is not active Hotel menu; no current API readiness claim.\n`;
reports.AI_PLANNER_AUDIT=pre('AI planner and itinerary audit')+`## Evidence\n\nCurrent provider is OpenAI; no Meta adapter found. Unit/contracts cover structured JSON schema, geographical/date/transport context, prompt safety, retries/timeouts, fact/quote constraints, costs, preservation of paid/manual items and failed-result quota behavior (see individual UNIT rows). Source mocks are not twelve live itinerary generations.\n\nLive display translation of an existing Indonesian itinerary completed in English with30January–1February2027, summaries/notes translated, original user prompt preserved.10successful-result quota remained. Month/weekday instruction and cachev2 fixed stale mixed language. Source validation preserves numeric facts, identifiers,URLs and prices; supplier/place proper names remain. Unknown historical route-placeholder fields may remain original-language: LOC-01.\n\nExisting saved trip read/reopen and edit modal open/close were verified; no save/delete/paid-toggle/regenerate action on owner data. Budget model/paid-item protection and multi-city application are contract-tested. Whole-trip duplicate/export/share/delete and Meta collaboration are NOT_IMPLEMENTED.\n\n## Profile coverage\n\nBudget,luxury,family,solo,multi-city,multi-country,flexible/fixed dates,hotel/budget/transport changes and regeneration all have explicit NOT_TESTED live rows. A disposable account/itinerary is required to run these without consuming owner entitlement or overwriting records. No invented live price/confirmed-booking claim is approved by this audit. Historic AI recommendations can still contain stale or unverified supplier facts; source labels must remain visible.\n`;
reports.PAYMENT_AUDIT=pre('Payment audit')+`## Midtrans\n\nBackend contracts test auth/origin,amount/signature reconciliation,idempotency/duplicates,pending/failure/expiration/cancel behavior,server-side status and entitlement activation. Wrong-signature/origin/unauthenticated production/local probes reject with403/401. Frontend redirect is not proof of settlement. No real production charge and no current isolated sandbox Snap transaction executed.\n\n## Nuitée SDK\n\nSeparate financial product from Trip Pass. Native room/session/change-of-terms/final amount/consent/status/recovery contracts pass. Current local history503 handled in readable English; full checkout shell ID/EN sampled seven widths. Historical owner SDK form rendered with Indonesia; this does not verify authorization/3DS,Book or refund. Owner payment tab was not operated and no guest data/terms/real card were submitted.\n\n## Required controlled validation\n\nOwner provisions sandbox configuration outside production and disposable payment user; exercise pending→success/failure/expired/cancel,duplicate submission/webhook,reconciliation and pass entitlement. For supplier checkout, owner operates any consequential payment/terms; verify confirmed booking reference and uncertain-state recovery before marking live-ready. Check LAS-3185 liability and payout terms separately. No approval flag or financial config was changed during QA.\n`;
reports.TRIP_PASS_AUDIT=pre('Trip Pass audit')+`## Actual product specification\n\nNew purchases30,000IDR/30days/10successfulAIresults shared account-wide across trips. Legacy20-result rights and older invoices retain original conditions. This supersedes the master checklist's hypothetical one-trip entitlement; do not reintroduce per-trip limits. Failed generation should not consume results. Expiry/exhaustion permit appropriate repurchase; manual editing remains available.\n\nFixtures cover access,quota,payment lifecycle,legacy preservation and unauthorized use. Existing owner UI reported10results and reload preservedsession; no entitlement grant/reset/purchase performed. Read-only access/status requests now carry language and checkout fallback translates. Live failed/exhausted/expired states remain synthetic; current sandbox settlement/activation and deployed migration/ownership must be verified in controlled accounts. Price Watch eligibility follows valid pass, not proof of a delivered alert.\n`;
reports.PRICE_WATCH_AUDIT=pre('Price Watch audit')+`## Verdict: PARTIAL — not certified working end to end\n\nFlight watch linked to saved itinerary, baseline then new-low comparison, own-account in-app notifications and optional verified-user Resend email. Hourly sourceCron, claim batch5,leases,eligibility/date expiry and email idempotency; support outbox every2minutes does not run flights. SQL supports2–14day trips. No hotel monitoring,arbitrary threshold,full price-history chart,increase alerts or Telegram price alerts found.\n\nBrowser existing watch displayed “Last checked:23/10/2026,05:00:28” and “No fare data yet”; notifications empty. This is persisted state, not a witnessed scheduled job/receipt. No watch created/stopped and no real email sent. Remote currentCron/appliedSQL remain unverified.\n\n## Fixed / exercised\n\nLegacy scope international now normalized to all for exact domestic routes. One DB finish error no longer abandons later claims. Email network failure defers one notice while continuing others, preserving Idempotency-Key. Tests cover claimed route/fare shape,no-price behavior,multi-watch isolation,synthetic drop noticeemail content and duplicates; SQL source reviews comparison/expiration/RLS. Full scheduled→provider→DB→alert→receipt is OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED.\n\n## Controlled acceptance procedure\n\n1.Owner designates a disposable watch,active pass and test email.\n2.Verify remote hourly trigger and effective account-scoped RPC grants; do not reapply historical SQL blindly.\n3.Witness one due baseline with exact route/date andlast_checked; inject an isolated synthetic lower fare in a test deployment.\n4.Assert exactly one own-account notification and one controlled email with correctIDR amount/date/link; unchanged/increase/unavailable/timeout must not fabricate drops.\n5.Replay/retry to establish dedupe; expire pass/date and prove no further processing; clean only designated disposable data.\n\nUntil that evidence exists, do not market reliable alert delivery as verified.\n`;
reports.TELEGRAM_SUPPORT_AUDIT=pre('Telegram support and task-agent audit')+`## Separation verified in source/contracts\n\nInternal task bot: allowlisted owner commands,queue validation/cancel/resume boundaries,tempqueue tests. Actual autonomous Desktop bridge remains unverified; no real task queue/secret file read or modified. Natural-language tasks are not shell authorization.\n\nCustomer support: separate webhook secret/bot/admin chat,validated text ticket creation,persistence,polling,adminreply/statusclose,outbox retries/rate limits/deduplication,recognizable credential/card rejection. Customer messages never execute internal developer commands. English admin footer corrected. Production support/config enabledtrue; localfalse. These are configuration flags, not live connectivity or conversation proof.\n\nNo customer/admin message was sent. Controlled create→notify→reply→user poll→close is OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED. Text two-way code exists, so it is PARTIAL rather than “one-way only” or “fully working”.\n\n## Missing support extensions and implementation plan\n\nComplaint category selector,screenshot upload and explicitreopen control not found. Add validated categoryenum (hotel,flight,transport,payment,TripPass,PriceWatch,AI,account,refund,technical,feedback) to frontend/API/DB with backwards-compatible general default; no customer text as code. For attachments, first define size/type quotas,malware/content checks,private storage,RLS and expiring owner-only access; never forward arbitrary URLs or credentials. Reopen must enforce ticketownership,rate limits and audit history. Migration/retention/security design must be reviewed before connecting real customers.\n`;
reports.SECURITY_AUDIT=pre('Security audit')+`## Bounded findings\n\nFull npm audit0known advisories (evidence/npm-audit.json), not proof of no vulnerabilities. Limited source/build pattern scan across${inventory.inventory.length}selectedfiles found0private-key/service-roleJWT/privateAPIkey patterns.42env names only were inventoried. No env/dev.vars/secret/queue/git-history files read; no secret values output. This is not an exhaustive historical secret scan.\n\nAuth/origin/webhook negative HTTP probes pass. Contracts cover trustedHTTPS hosts,query validation,SSRF/redirect constraints,provider failure sanitization,unsafe AIoutput,booking price/consent/status guards,payment amount/signature and idempotency,support authorization/rate/privacy rules. Parameterized Supabase APIs and RLS source reviewed. DeployedDB policies/two-account isolation, token refresh and external account/WAF security not attested.\n\nReact text rendering reduces direct HTML injection; this is not a complete XSS audit. Vendor affiliate scripts and sandboxed third-party widgets remain supply-chain dependencies. Several static pages lack security headers (SEC-01); enforce a tested allowlist/report-only CSP before production enforcement to avoid breaking official SDK/widgets. No destructive penetration test or third-party attack run.\n\nNo observedP0; P1 payment/RLS verification gaps remain. Source credentials are server-side as reviewed, but no claim about supplier compromise or universal immunity is made.\n`;
reports.UX_UI_AUDIT=pre('UX, accessibility and SEO audit')+`## Executed browser coverage\n\n${responsive.length} top-level overflow samples across${new Set(responsive.map(x=>x.view)).size}views at320,375,390,768,1024,1440,1920px; no horizontal document overflow in these samples. ID/EN homepage/help/flights/Trip.com/transport/saved/planner/map/costs/nativehotel/PriceWatch/editdialog/policies/checkout shells are represented. ${actions.length} recorded browser interactions cover dialogs,10FAQ entries,empty search,one-way/autocomplete/details,language persistence,mobile dropdown,trip read,Google WALK,translation,budgetvalidation,legalnavigation and12Go readiness. Screenshots accompany320/1440samples.\n\nDOM image-alt scan found0missingalt in sampled top-level views. Modal rawDOM unnamed-button metric1 is not itself a confirmed defect: accessibility tree showed named modalcontrols and the scan includes background/inert content. No comprehensive cross-origin iframe alt/focus,screenreader,colorcontrast or touch-target certification. Payments/consent/delete/save/register/logout were not executed on owner account.\n\n## Findings\n\nEnglish plural/category/CTA/geography/narrative month and aria labels fixed; ID/EN forms remain responsive. True404 and crawl files pass locally. Production unknownpage/crawl responses remain FAIL pending owner release. Header navigation is in-memory:refresh returnsExplore while language/session/draft persist; browserback/forward verified on real policyURLs. This behavior is documented rather than falsely claiming deep-linking of every view.\n\nExpired/empty checkout does not start a payment. Local not-ready error is translated; an empty checkout lacks a dedicated FindhotelCTA beyond Returnhome (P3improvement). Native realpayment form full3DS/confirmUI cannot be recreated safely on ownerproductionrecord. Original ownerpaymenttab preserved.\n`;
reports.PERFORMANCE_AUDIT=pre('Performance and reliability audit')+`## Measurements\n\nBuild evidence final:entryJS about966.13kB minified/288.46kB gzip; CSS156.18kB/33.44kB gzip; lazyleaflet148.60kB/43.32kB gzip. Build2.88s on this machine; this is not a user-page timing. Chunkwarning>500kB remains.\n\nReal supplier elapsed samples:Yogyakartasearch6307ms,content1209ms,Viatorproduction2035ms,flight389–738ms in the recorded batch. HTTP JSON stores perrequest timings. These are single warm/cold mixed samples,notp95,SLA or loadbenchmark. No productionbulkload.\n\nCurrent console summary captured2warning/error entries; rawmessages/URLs not retained to avoid sensitive diagnostic data. The local checkout503 was expected during unavailable-state testing; no blanket “console clean” claim. Browser hydration/map rendering otherwise visually sampled.\n\nTimeouts,retries,invalidproviders,duplicateactions and cache/identity handling have mock regression coverage. No reproducibleLCP/INP/CLS,heapmemory,networkthrottle/offline ormultidevicehardwareprofile taken; markedNOT_TESTED. Recommend route/component splitting and actual coldmobileprofiling before setting performance acceptance thresholds.\n`;
reports.OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED=pre('Owner-controlled acceptance actions')+mdTable(['ID','Required verification','Exact blocker'],manual.filter(x=>x.status==='OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED').map(x=>[x.id,x.title,x.detail]))+`\n## Priorities and boundaries\n\n1.Isolated sandbox payment+two-userRLS validation before unrestricted paidlaunch.\n2.Controlled scheduledPriceWatch andTelegramroundtrip tests before promisingdelivery.\n3.Review privacy wording and deploylocalfixes only on explicitownerreleaseinstruction.\n4.Verify backup/restore,remoteCron,migrationorder,billingprojectquotas and conversion/payout when relevant.\n\nDo not send APIkeys/passwords/OTP/carddata through chat. No need to re-register Nuitée, republish5%margin,reactivateGoogle,or fixWhite-label for currentproductpath. LAS-3147 is archival,not a launch gate. LAS-3185 is a separate account-card/commercial issue and remains unanswered in suppliedevidence.\n\nLegalreview: privacy whole-tripdeleteclaim vs availableitemdelete, embeddedSDK vs generalpartner-sitebookingwording, and ambiguousGoogleexternal-servicephrase. No legalmeaning changed automatically. The engineeringaudit can close with these explicitblockedcases; payment/notification readiness cannot be calledPASS without actualevidence.\n`;
reports.FIX_LOG=pre('QA fix log')+fixTable+`\n## Remaining issues\n\n`+issueTable+`\n## Change boundaries\n\nPre-existing hotel/flightbudget/regional work remains in the branch and has regression coverage, but is not counted as newly discovered QA bugs. Unrelated WORKFLOW.md deletion,untracked envexample/artifacts/unrelatedrootfile were preserved. No staging/commit/push/deploy. npm audit did not alter packages. Final typecheck/build and259fixtures pass.\n`;
reports.PRODUCTION_READINESS=pre('Production readiness decision')+`## Decision\n\n**NO-GO: unrestricted native paidbooking/payment launch.** Payment/booking end-to-end,sandboxTripPasssettlement,deployedRLSisolation and scheduledalertdelivery are not established. These are verification gaps,not proof of a provider failure. No observedP0underboundedreview.\n\n**CONDITIONAL GO: limited discovery/affiliate browsing**, only with source-labelled cached/estimated/fromprices, no reservation or alert-reliability guarantees, clear provider handoff and existing safeguards. Local QAfixes are not yet released. Owner must decide exposure of financially unverified flows; this audit did not disable/changeproductionsettings.\n\n`+mdTable(['Area','Assessment'],features.filter(x=>!['White-label Nuitée','Klook','Meta collaboration'].includes(x[0])).map(x=>[x[0],x[1]+' — '+x[2]]))+`\n## Release acceptance\n\nApply localnonfinancialQAfixes after review and explicitreleaseinstruction; rerunproduction404/robots/sitemapandcriticalroute/authsmoke. VerifyeffectiveRLS/RPCmigrationstateandcontrolledtwo-userisolation. CompleteisolatedMidtranssandboxlifecycleandowner-operatedNuitéeSDKBook/recoveryonlywithappropriateauthorization. EstablishPriceWatchscheduledalertreceiptandcontrolledsupportconversation. Profilemobileperformanceandreviewprivacywording. Preserve rollbackversion8f76d368-5417-4498-a44f-ee7c038e5a19 as historicalreference; freshremoteversionattestationnotperformed.\n\nWhite-label403 is excluded from gates by latest ownerinstruction. Do not delay activeAPI+SDK solelyforLAS-3147.\n`;
reports.ENGLISH_LOCALIZATION_AUDIT=pre('English language and localization audit')+`## Coverage and result\n\nPARTIAL overall; safe corrections applied and affected regression/UI checks rerun. ${coverage.keys}dictionarykeys/${coverage.staticCalls}staticcalls with0coverageerrors and0unapprovedliteraltexts;3intentionalbrandoccurrences (Viator twice andSORTTRIP·HOTEL·TRIP.COM). This lexicalauditdoesnot certify allruntimebranches. ID/EN switching,persistence,title/documentlanguage,formlabels,currencies,counts,policyarticlesandmultiplelayoutsverified. Top-level responsive evidence includes both languages.\n\n## Corrections by surface\n\n`+fixTable+`\n## Formatting and dynamic content\n\nEnglish usesen-GB; ID usesid-ID; currencyIDR unchanged (e.g.IDR300,000 vsRp300.000), suppliercurrency/amounts preserved. Dates use localizedmonthformats where formatted,withISOvaluesin nativeinput/savedrawdatefields; timezone indicationAsia/Jakarta/device time and origin-time labels retained. Some historical returnflight/savedcards showISOdate/time as a stableunambiguousformat rather than fullyfriendlylocalizeddate. Browser-nativepickercontrols may followdeviceOSlanguage independently ofapp.\n\nLive AItranslation now30January–1February2027,routeprose translated; originaluserprompt,properplacenames,sourceURLs,numericfactsandfinancialconditions notrewritten. Historicunknownplaceholdermode/location strings and manualuserprose remainpotentialsource-languageexceptions. Failedtranslationdisplaysretry rather than fabricatedEnglish. Newcachev2invalidatesoldmixedmonthresults.\n\n## Notifications and transactional content\n\nEnglishPriceWatchemail fixture has naturalfare-drop copy,unchangedIDRamounts/bookingURL and one-adultscope. Supportnoticefooter followslanguage; customeroriginaltextretained. No liveemail/Telegrammessage or postpaymentbookingconfirmation was sent, so actual deliverylocale and fullsupplierconfirmationtext remainOWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED. TripPassreadrequests andfallback nowlocalized; conditionalbranches coveredbycontracts,notlivefinancialE2E.\n\n## Legal / vendor exceptions\n\nPreserved cancellation,refund,payment,andprivacymeaning. LEGAL-01requiresownerreviewofprivacydeleteclaim/SDKwording/ambiguousexternal-servicephrase. VendorTrip.com“0Children”and12GoEnglishforminIDshellarenotrewritteninsidecrossoriginframes. Supplierreviews/roomnamescanremainoriginallanguage; donotpretendtheyweretranslated. InternationalEnglishtravellerterminologyupdatedinownedmicrocopy; legalhistoricaltraveler/travelingvariantsflaggedforcopyreviewwithoutsubstantiverewrite. Englishaudit is not a claimofzeroIndonesianinallhistoricaluserdata/providercontent.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nregression-tests.tap259PASS; localization-coverage.json; ui-actions.json; ui-responsive.json; native-hotel-{id,en}screenshots; privacy-en/terms-en; checkout-empty-id/checkout-unavailable-en; planner-en/map-en and finalhomeID. Fresh-build aria labels checkedEnglish. Readinesslimits are explicit in QA_TEST_MATRIX.csv.\n`;
