reports.ENGLISH_LOCALIZATION_AUDIT=pre('English language and localization audit')+`## Coverage and result

PARTIAL overall. Safe corrections were applied and regression/UI checks were rerun. The static audit found ${coverage.keys} dictionary keys and ${coverage.staticCalls} calls, with zero coverage errors and zero unapproved literal texts. Three brand occurrences are intentional: Viator twice and SORTTRIP · HOTEL · TRIP.COM. Static coverage does not establish every runtime branch.

English and Indonesian switching, persistence, document language, titles, form labels, currency formatting, counts, policy articles and responsive layouts were checked. Details and evidence are in the test matrix; skipped financial and messaging states are not counted as passing UI tests.

## Corrections by surface

`+fixTable+`
## Dates, currencies and dynamic content

English uses en-GB; Indonesian uses id-ID. The currency remains IDR: for example, IDR 300,000 in English and Rp300.000 in Indonesian. Supplier amounts and currencies were preserved. Formatted dates use localized month names; native date inputs and some historical saved cards retain unambiguous ISO values. Device time zone and flight origin-time labels remain visible. Browser date-picker controls can follow the operating system language independently of the application.

Live translation of the existing itinerary now displays “30 January–1 February 2027” and translated route descriptions. Original user prompts, proper place names, URLs and numeric facts are preserved. The translation cache was advanced to v2 so old mixed-language month names do not persist. Failed translations offer a retry rather than fabricated English. Some historical unknown mode/location placeholders and user-written prose can still remain in their original language; this is a recorded limitation, not a complete localization pass.

## Notifications, booking and payment

The English Price Watch email fixture uses natural fare-drop copy and preserves IDR amounts, the booking URL and the one-adult scope. The Telegram support notice footer follows the ticket language; the original customer message is retained. No real email, Telegram message or financial booking confirmation was sent, so delivery language and supplier confirmation text remain unverified.

Trip Pass access/status polling now sends the selected language, and the configuration fallback is localized. Both language modes were checked on the native hotel form and checkout shell. The local unavailable-checkout response is readable English. Payment authorization, 3DS and final booking confirmations were not exercised on a real production transaction.

## Legal and provider exceptions

Cancellation, refund, payment and privacy meaning was preserved. LEGAL-01 requires owner review: the privacy policy mentions whole-trip deletion that was not found in the UI; general partner-site booking wording needs reconciliation with the embedded SDK section; the phrase “where the external service applies” is ambiguous. No substantive legal rewrite was made.

Trip.com's “0 Children” and the 12Go English form in an Indonesian shell are provider-controlled copy. Supplier reviews and room names can remain in their original language. These cross-origin widgets and original user text were not silently rewritten. Owned microcopy uses international English with “traveller”; historical “traveler/traveling” variants in legal prose are flagged for a later copy review.

## Verification

All 259 automated regressions passed. Evidence includes localization-coverage.json, ui-actions.json, ui-responsive.json and screenshots under 2026-10-23/evidence. Fresh-build accessible labels for booking, item information and prices were observed in English. The layout metric checks the top-level document; it does not certify every provider frame, all screen-reader behavior or WCAG conformance. See the matrix for exact exclusions.
`;
reports.OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED=pre('Owner-controlled acceptance actions')+mdTable(['ID','Required verification','Exact blocker'],manual.filter(x=>x.status==='OWNER_ACTION_REQUIRED').map(x=>[x.id,x.title,x.detail]))+`
## Priorities

1. Prepare an isolated Midtrans sandbox and disposable users; verify settlement, entitlement and two-user RLS before unrestricted paid launch.
2. Observe a controlled scheduled Price Watch alert and a controlled Telegram support round trip before promising delivery.
3. Review privacy wording. Deploy local fixes only after explicit release authorization, then repeat the production smoke checks.
4. Verify backup/restore, remote Cron, migration order, billing-project quotas and affiliate attribution where relevant.

No API keys, passwords, OTPs or card details are needed in chat. Do not repeat Nuitée registration, publication of the existing 5% margin or Google activation. White-label LAS-3147 is archival and is not a launch gate. LAS-3185 remains a separate commercial question about the account card; no substantive answer is present in the supplied evidence.

Legal review is also required for the privacy deletion claim, native SDK wording and ambiguous Google external-service phrase. The engineering audit can close with these explicit boundaries. Payments and notification delivery cannot be marked PASS without the missing evidence.
`;
reports.PERFORMANCE_AUDIT=pre('Performance and reliability audit')+`## Measurements

The final build produces approximately 966 kB of entry JavaScript (288 kB gzip), 156 kB of CSS (33 kB gzip) and a lazy Leaflet chunk of 149 kB (43 kB gzip). Vite still reports an entry chunk larger than 500 kB. Exact sizes and build duration are in build-final.log; build time is not page-load performance.

Recorded supplier elapsed samples: Yogyakarta hotel search 6,307 ms, content 1,209 ms, production Viator 2,035 ms and flight searches 290–738 ms. These are individual mixed warm/cold samples, not p95 latency, an SLA or a load benchmark. HTTP probe JSON includes individual timings. No high-volume production load test was run.

The console summary captured two warning/error entries. Raw messages and URLs were not retained to avoid sensitive diagnostic data. Local checkout readiness 503 was deliberately exercised; no blanket claim of a clean console is made.

Timeouts, retries, invalid provider responses, duplicate actions and cache/identity handling have mock regression coverage. LCP, INP, CLS, heap memory, throttled/offline networking and physical-device profiling are NOT_TESTED. Split the large application bundle where measurements justify it, then profile a cold mobile load before setting acceptance thresholds.
`;
reports.PRODUCTION_READINESS=pre('Production readiness decision')+`## Decision

**NO-GO for unrestricted native booking/payment launch.** The complete payment/booking lifecycle, isolated Trip Pass sandbox settlement, deployed two-user RLS isolation and scheduled alert delivery have not been established. These are verification gaps, not proof that the providers have failed. No P0 was observed in this bounded audit.

**CONDITIONAL GO for limited discovery and affiliate browsing.** Keep cached fares, estimates, starting prices and provider handoffs clearly labelled. Do not promise a reservation or reliable alert delivery without supporting evidence. Local QA changes are not released. This audit did not change production exposure or financial settings.

`+mdTable(['Area','Assessment'],features.filter(x=>!['White-label Nuitée','Klook','Meta collaboration'].includes(x[0])).map(x=>[x[0],x[1]+' — '+x[2]]))+`
## Release acceptance

Review the local fixes and release only on explicit instruction. After release, repeat the production unknown-page 404, robots, sitemap, checkout and authentication smoke checks. Verify the effective RLS/RPC migration state with controlled accounts. Complete the isolated Midtrans lifecycle and any owner-operated Nuitée SDK booking/recovery test with appropriate authorization. Establish scheduled Price Watch receipt and a controlled support conversation. Review privacy wording, static security headers, backup/restore evidence and mobile performance.

Historical rollback reference: 8f76d368-5417-4498-a44f-ee7c038e5a19. A fresh remote-version attestation was not performed. White-label 403 is excluded from release gates by the latest owner instruction; the active API + SDK path does not depend on LAS-3147.
`;
